        "original_id": "5c9bed47-efbc-5985-aa80-b2e2f44ae1e5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Klete Keller, Michael Phelps, Ryan Lochte, Peter Vanderkaay, Young Jeezy, Detail, Akon, Ray J, Lil Wayne, Beyoncé, Wiz Khalifa\n- Events: Athens games\n- Songs: \"I'm So Paid\", \"Sexy Can I\", \"How to Love\", \"Drunk in Love\", \"711\", \"We Dem Boyz\"\n- Roles: Olympian, swimmer, record producer\n\nFacts:\n- Since the Athens games, the American relay of Michael Phelps, Ryan Lochte, Peter Vanderkaay, and Klete Keller has remained undefeated.\n- Michael Fred Phelps II was born on June 30, 1985.\n- Michael Phelps is an American former competitive swimmer.\n- Michael Phelps is the most decorated Olympian of all time with 28 total medals.\n- Fellow Olympian Michael Phelps is referenced in Young Jeezy's verse on the song \"I'm So Paid.\"\n- Record producer Detail is perhaps best known for producing hit singles including \"Sexy Can I\" by Ray J, \"I'm So Paid\" by Akon, \"How to Love\" by Lil Wayne, \"Drunk in Love\" and \"711\" by Beyoncé, and \"We Dem Boyz\" by Wiz Khalifa.",
